WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.660 --> 00:00:02.300
Hey, this is Presh Talwalkar.

00:00:02.840 --> 00:00:05.260
An evil warden holds you prisoner,

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:07.700
but offers you a chance
to escape.

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:12.500
There are three doors A, B, and C.

00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:15.220
Two of the doors lead to freedom

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:18.400
and the third door
leads to lifetime imprisonment,

00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:21.660
but you do not know 
which door is what type.

00:00:22.840 --> 00:00:24.720
You are allowed to point
to a door

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:28.100
and ask a single yes/no question
to the warden.

00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:32.400
If you point to a door
that leads to freedom,

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:35.740
the warden does answer
your question truthfully,

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:40.560
but if you point to the door
that leads to imprisonment,

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:43.780
the warden answers
your question randomly,

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:47.120
either saying yes or no
by chance.

00:00:48.980 --> 00:00:50.460
Can you think of a question

00:00:50.460 --> 00:00:53.140
and figure out a way to escape for sure?

00:00:54.060 --> 00:00:56.100
Give this problem a try,
and when you're ready,

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:58.540
keep watching the video
for the solution.

00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:11.320
So here's a way that you 
can escape for sure.

00:01:12.540 --> 00:01:16.100
Point to door A
and ask the question,

00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:19.360
"Does Door B lead to freedom?"

00:01:21.380 --> 00:01:25.340
If the warden answers "Yes,"
then pick door B.

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:30.040
If the warden answers "No,"
then pick door C.

00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:34.180
This strategy is guaranteed to work

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:37.400
regardless of the door type
of A.

00:01:39.480 --> 00:01:40.880
So why does it work?

00:01:41.660 --> 00:01:43.540
Let's work through the logic.

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:47.320
Door A can either have
two different types.

00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:50.000
It can either lead to freedom,

00:01:50.180 --> 00:01:52.300
in which case the
warden is truthful,

00:01:52.700 --> 00:01:54.380
or it can lead to imprisonment,

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:57.180
in which case the warden
answers randomly.

00:01:58.420 --> 00:02:01.800
Let's consider the first case,
that the door leads to freedom.

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:07.280
In this case, if the warden
answers "Yes" to your question,

00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:10.200
then that means the warden is
answering truthfully,

00:02:10.420 --> 00:02:12.880
and Door B does lead
to freedom.

00:02:14.120 --> 00:02:18.000
Similarly, if the warden says Door B
does not lead to freedom,

00:02:18.160 --> 00:02:20.020
the warden is answering truthfully,

00:02:20.220 --> 00:02:22.400
which means door B
leads to imprisonment.

00:02:22.780 --> 00:02:26.520
That means the other door,
door C, leads to freedom.

00:02:27.740 --> 00:02:30.160
So you can see that
if the warden answers "Yes,"

00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:31.420
you should pick door B,

00:02:31.540 --> 00:02:34.600
and if the warden answers "No,"
then you should pick door C.

00:02:35.240 --> 00:02:38.800
But what about the case
where door A leads to imprisonment,

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:41.020
and the warden answers randomly?

00:02:42.020 --> 00:02:45.180
Well, in this case, if door A
leads to imprisonment,

00:02:45.380 --> 00:02:49.800
that means the other two doors,
B and C, lead to freedom.

00:02:50.460 --> 00:02:53.340
So you can always pick doors
B and C in these cases

00:02:53.340 --> 00:02:55.340
no matter what the warden answers.

00:02:55.960 --> 00:02:58.960
So if you pick door B
when the warden answers "Yes,"

00:02:59.160 --> 00:03:00.460
that will lead to freedom,

00:03:00.700 --> 00:03:03.100
and you pick door C when the
warden answers "No,"

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:05.140
that once again
will lead to freedom.

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:08.640
So this shows that logically,

00:03:08.940 --> 00:03:11.540
if you pick door B when the
warden answers "Yes,"

00:03:11.780 --> 00:03:14.140
and if you pick door C
when the warden answers "No,"

00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:15.760
you are guaranteed to

00:03:15.760 --> 00:03:18.460
find a door that leads you to freedom.

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:20.680
Did you figure it out?

